---
import Ledger from "./Ledger.astro";
import Numeral from "./Numeral.astro";
import Spread from "./Spread.astro";

const training = [
  { source: "Development", action: "Train the weights", result: "model.bin", detail: "Labeled corpus rows" },
  { source: "Validation", action: "Set the boundary", result: "boundary + scale", detail: "Uses weights and rules" },
  { source: "Lexicon", action: "Compile the rules", result: "language rule pack", detail: "Conservative entries" },
];
const points = [
  ["Lexicon hit", "30", "A conservative entry alone stays below the warning threshold."],
  ["Targeted hit", "70", "A lexicon hit with a nearby target, such as you."],
  ["Identity attack", "85", "An identity entry with a nearby group word."],
  ["Hostile wish", "85", "A frame such as I hope you die."],
  ["Direct threat", "95", "A frame such as I will kill you."],
];
---
<Spread id="mechanism" label="the mechanism · how it works" class="wide">
  <div class="stage">
    <header class="mechanism-intro">
      <div>
        <Numeral value="III" />
        <p class="rubric">chapter three · how it works</p>
        <h2 id="mechanism-title" class="title">Two channels.<br />One verdict.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="copy">Blasphem hashes word and character n-grams into sparse feature vectors. A linear classifier trained offline scores them with 16-bit weights.</p>
        <p class="copy">Lexicons and context rules contribute to the verdict. Detection runs locally without neural networks or cloud inference.</p>
        <a class="source-link" href="https://github.com/sospedra/blasphem/blob/main/HOW.md">Read HOW.md <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="diagrams">
      <figure class="diagram" aria-labelledby="training-title">
        <svg class="ornament" viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#quatrefoil"></use></svg>
        <figcaption id="training-title"><span class="rubric">I · before it ships</span><h3>From corpus to engine</h3></figcaption>
        <p class="diagram-caption">Language corpora and conservative lexica.</p>
        <div class="training-branches">
          {training.map((branch) => (
            <div class="training-branch">
              <h4>{branch.source}</h4>
              <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
              <p>{branch.action}<small>{branch.detail}</small></p>
              <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
              <code>{branch.result}</code>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div class="merge" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="engine-node"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 26" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#cross"></use></svg><span>Compiled engine + data</span></div>
        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        <div class="test-node"><span>Test split</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>Judge every row</span></div>
        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        <div class="benchmark-node"><span>Measured precision & recall</span><a href="#test-benchmark">Read the benchmark ↗</a></div>
        <p class="diagram-note">Test rows measure results. They never train weights or select the boundary.</p>
      </figure>

      <figure class="diagram runtime" aria-labelledby="runtime-title">
        <svg class="ornament" viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#quatrefoil"></use></svg>
        <figcaption id="runtime-title"><span class="rubric">II · on your device</span><h3>From message to verdict</h3></figcaption>
        <div class="message-node">Your message</div>
        <div class="fork" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="channels">
          <div class="channel"><span class="channel-mark">A</span><h4>Model</h4><p>Word and character patterns</p><strong>0–100</strong><span>evidence score</span></div>
          <div class="channel"><span class="channel-mark">B</span><h4>Rules</h4><p>Lexicon hits and sentence context</p><strong>0–100</strong><span>rule points</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="suppression"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span><p><b>Context can suppress a hit.</b><br />Suppression caps the model at 49. Other rule evidence can still trigger a warning.</p></div>
        <div class="merge" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="verdict-node"><code>max(model, rules) ≥ 50</code><strong>Flag the message</strong><span>Otherwise, return safe.</span></div>
        <p class="diagram-note">The SDK returns a score from 0 to 1. Its warning threshold is 0.5.</p>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="mechanism-notes">
      <div><h3>A small, trained model</h3><p class="copy">Each model uses 65,536 integer weights. Training compresses word and character evidence into a 131 KB artifact.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Context matters</h3><p class="copy">Negation, quotation, reporting, and counterspeech can suppress a hit. A word alone does not always justify a warning.</p></div>
      <div><h3>One explicit boundary</h3><p class="copy">Calibration selects the boundary on validation rows. It favors precision and limits warnings on clean messages.</p></div>
    </div>

    <details class="scoring-details">
      <summary>Rule points and calibration gates</summary>
      <p class="copy">Spanish uses the full policy frames below. The other 14 languages use the static rule tables. Their lexicon hits add 30 points and cannot flag a message alone.</p>
      <Ledger id="rule-points" caption="Rule channel · evidence points" columns={["Evidence", "Points", "Context"]} rows={points} prose={[2]} source="https://github.com/sospedra/blasphem/blob/main/HOW.md#rule-channel" />
      <p class="copy">A validation boundary must keep false warnings at or below 3% and precision at or above 90%. It must also keep every clean control below the warning threshold.</p>
      <p class="copy">These are calibration gates. The separate test benchmark reports measured performance after calibration.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</Spread>

<style>
  .mechanism-intro { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 64px; align-items: end; margin-bottom: 48px; }
  .mechanism-intro :global(.numeral) { font-size: 110px; margin: 0 0 24px; }
  .mechanism-intro .copy { font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .source-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; gap: 12px; color: var(--bone); text-underline-offset: 5px; text-decoration-color: var(--blood-hair); }
  .diagrams { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 28px; }
  .diagram { position: relative; min-width: 0; margin: 0; padding: 34px 24px 24px; border: 1px solid var(--blood-hair); background: var(--pitch); text-align: center; }
  .ornament { position: absolute; width: 24px; height: 24px; top: -12px; left: calc(50% - 12px); background: var(--pitch); color: var(--blood); }
  figcaption .rubric { font-size: 10px; }
  h3 { margin: 10px 0 0; font: 400 31px/1.1 var(--font-goth); color: var(--bone); }
  .diagram-caption, .diagram-note { color: var(--taupe-ink); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.4; }
  .diagram-caption { margin: 12px 0 28px; }
  .diagram-note { margin: 22px auto 0; max-width: 42ch; }
  .training-branches { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 10px; }
  .training-branch { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; min-width: 0; }
  .training-branch h4 { margin: 0; padding: 10px 3px; border: 1px solid var(--hair); font: 400 20px/1.15 var(--font-goth); }
  .training-branch p { margin: 0; min-height: 76px; padding: 8px 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.25; color: var(--parchment); }
  .training-branch small { display: block; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.3; color: var(--taupe-ink); }
  .training-branch code { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 54px; padding: 7px; border: 1px solid var(--hair); background: var(--coal); font: 10px/1.5 var(--font-mono); color: var(--parchment); }
  .flow-arrow { display: block; color: var(--blood-ink); font: 22px/30px var(--font-body); }
  .merge { height: 24px; width: 67%; margin: 0 auto 24px; border: 1px solid var(--blood-hair); border-top: 0; position: relative; }
  .merge::after { content: ""; position: absolute; height: 24px; width: 1px; background: var(--blood-hair); top: 100%; left: 50%; }
  .engine-node { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 12px; padding: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--blood-hair); background: #231617; font: 400 23px/1.2 var(--font-goth); }
  .engine-node svg { width: 12px; height: 18px; fill: var(--blood-ink); }
  .test-node { display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; gap: 16px; padding: 12px; border: 1px dashed var(--hair); color: var(--parchment); font-size: 15px; }
  .test-node > span:nth-child(2) { color: var(--blood-ink); }
  .benchmark-node { padding: 14px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--hair); }
  .benchmark-node > span { display: block; font: 400 23px/1.2 var(--font-goth); }
  .benchmark-node a { display: inline-block; padding-top: 8px; color: var(--blood-ink); font: 10px/1.6 var(--font-mono); text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .message-node { margin: 28px auto 0; padding: 12px 26px; width: fit-content; border: 1px solid var(--hair); font: 400 23px var(--font-goth); }
  .fork { height: 24px; width: 52%; margin: 24px auto 0; border: 1px solid var(--blood-hair); border-bottom: 0; position: relative; }
  .fork::before { content: ""; width: 1px; height: 24px; position: absolute; bottom: 100%; left: 50%; background: var(--blood-hair); }
  .channels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px; }
  .channel { position: relative; padding: 22px 12px; border: 1px solid var(--hair); background: var(--coal); }
  .channel-mark { position: absolute; left: 10px; top: 8px; color: var(--blood-ink); font: 10px var(--font-rubric); }
  .channel h4 { margin: 0; font: 400 30px/1.2 var(--font-goth); }
  .channel p { min-height: 44px; margin: 12px 0; color: var(--parchment); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.3; }
  .channel strong { display: block; color: var(--blood-ink); font: 400 33px/1 var(--font-goth); }
  .channel > span:last-child { display: block; margin-top: 10px; color: var(--taupe-ink); font: 10px var(--font-mono); }
  .suppression { display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: center; margin-top: 16px; padding: 12px; border: 1px dashed var(--blood-hair); }
  .suppression > span { font-size: 26px; color: var(--blood-ink); }
  .suppression p { margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--taupe-ink); }
  .suppression b { font-weight: 500; color: var(--parchment); }
  .verdict-node { padding: 20px 12px; border: 1px solid var(--blood-hair); background: #231617; }
  .verdict-node code { color: var(--taupe-ink); font: 11px var(--font-mono); }
  .verdict-node strong { display: block; margin: 10px 0 6px; color: var(--bone); font: 400 30px/1 var(--font-goth); }
  .verdict-node > span { color: var(--parchment); font-size: 15px; }
  .mechanism-notes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 32px; margin-top: 34px; }
  .mechanism-notes h3 { font-size: 26px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .mechanism-notes .copy { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .scoring-details { border-top: 1px solid var(--hair); margin-top: 24px; }
  summary { padding: 22px 0; cursor: pointer; font: 400 27px/1.3 var(--font-goth); }
  summary::marker { color: var(--blood-ink); }
  .scoring-details .copy { max-width: 84ch; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1200px) { .diagrams { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .mechanism-intro, .diagrams, .mechanism-notes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
    .mechanism-intro { gap: 8px; }
    .diagram { padding: 30px 16px 22px; }
    .training-branches { gap: 8px; }
    .training-branch h4 { font-size: 18px; }
    .training-branch p { min-height: 94px; font-size: 15px; }
    .training-branch code { font-size: 9px; }
    .mechanism-notes { gap: 12px; }
  }
</style>
